  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Life Saving Emergency Response to Tropical Cyclone Freddy affected Internally Displaced Persons (IDPs) in Mulanje, Phalombe and Blantyre Districts of Southern Malawi.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project provides Vulnerable Internally Displaced Persons in Camps in Mulanje, Phalombe, and Blantyre with cash for Shelter and Core Relief Items to support their basic needs. UNHCR implements profiling of the beneficiaries in the targeted districts, carries out market assessments to validate existing market data, Distributes cash to the beneficiaries, and Undertakes post-distribution monitoring. The project provides humanitarian assistance to 20,000 people, including 6,000 women, 3,000 men, 11,000 children, and including 180 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
